    "type": "question",
    "label": "76",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equations simultaneously for $x$ and $y$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}5^{x-y}&=25^x\\\\4^{x+2y}&=\\frac12\\end{aligned}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\dfrac12$, $y=-\\dfrac12$.\n\nEquate powers to obtain $y=-x$, then substitute into the other linear equation.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}5^{x-y}&=5^{2x}\\\\x-y&=2x\\\\y&=-x\\\\2^{2(x+2y)}&=2^{-1}\\\\2x+4y&=-1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute $y=-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}2x+4(-x)&=-1\\\\-2x&=-1\\\\x&=\\frac12\\\\y&=-\\frac12\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
